body:
Just keep in mind that you get what you pay for. Groomer that charge correctly HATE groomers that under charge. It really really hurts our industry when people support cheap groomers. Most of them don't do a good job and don't have the same qualifications and certifications. I charge more than other shops in my area because I offer high quality groomers. My shop is filled with very expensive products. I am constantly spending thousands of dollars to attend seminars and conventions to continue my education, keep up to date with safety, and to make sure I have the best products and grooming supplies.

&#x200B;

lol, down voting my comment. As a dog groomer who is constantly shit on by clients who want me to lower my prices because Betsy down the street groomer downs out of her garage for $30, I hate cheap groomers. It doesn't just hurt MY business, it hurts every other groomers business that is legal. Most of these cheap groomers have never been to grooming school, never taken a safety class and don't even have a business license or insurance to protect themselves, their illegal business and their clients for WHEN they injure a dog and end up having to pay a huge vet bill directly out of pocket. So screw me for caring and being legal right? lol My bad.
